WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.775
A live race now shares one board: positions and gaps for every rider, every second,

00:00:07.775 --> 00:00:09.139
from the service.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.333
The board is the service's: every rider by place, you in fifth, each gap to you,

00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:17.637
seven seconds up to five behind.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.431
Each second the race sends your distance and power to the session, never more than

00:00:27.431 --> 00:00:28.500
twice a second.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.123
The service rides the bots on the pace model, ranks by distance, and times each gap

00:00:41.123 --> 00:00:42.866
from the leader's trace.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.513
The board joins at tablet width and up; on a phone the race keeps your place beside

00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:54.352
the power.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.853
What the tests prove: one ranking for everyone, each gap to you, and reports at most

00:01:06.853 --> 00:01:08.030
twice a second.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.869
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.726
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.397
every hill and interval.

00:01:23.742 --> 00:01:28.920
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.368
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.358
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.196
A custom workout lives under Profile.
